# Mizaic Brand Kit Enforcement

Apply when writing any UI component, stylesheet, token file, or layout.
The Mizaic brand kit overrides all previous generic colour and font choices.

## Colour palette

| Role            | Hex      | Notes                                    |
|-----------------|----------|------------------------------------------|
| Primary         | #0d46d6  | Electric Blue. 6.02:1 on white -- AA ok  |
| Primary hover   | #002178  | Royal Blue                               |
| Primary dark    | #00093b  | Midnight Navy -- splash bg, dark surfaces|
| Secondary       | #9338ff  | Mizaic Violet                            |
| Secondary hover | #6600ab  | Mizaic Indigo                            |
| Brand accent    | #d758ff  | Magenta -- logo spinning-O only          |
| Accent blue     | #0071e2  | Blue 1 -- info states, links             |
| Light accent    | #0096fd  | Light Blue 1 -- focus ring on dark bg    |

All colours live in `services/design-system/src/tokens/color.ts`.
Import from `@leo/design-system` tokens. Never hardcode hex.

## Forbidden values

The old "generic blue" scheme is banned in new code:

- `#1F3A8A` -- old primary (replaced by #0d46d6)
- `#1D4ED8` -- old design-system brand primary (replaced by #0d46d6)
- `#0F766E` -- old secondary teal (replaced by #9338ff)
- `#1E40AF` -- old primary hover (replaced by #002178)
- `#152A66` -- old primary dark (replaced by #00093b)

If a pre-existing file still uses these values, add to the PR description
and track in `compliance/coverage-waivers.md`.

## Fonts

| Role            | Family        | Weights loaded     |
|-----------------|---------------|--------------------|
| Body / UI copy  | Albert Sans   | 300 400 500 600 700|
| Headlines (h1-h6)| Overpass     | 300 400 600 700    |
| Code / SNOMED   | JetBrains Mono| 400 500            |

Font CSS variables:
- Body: `var(--font-albert-sans)`
- Heading: `var(--font-overpass)`
- Mono: `var(--font-jetbrains-mono)`

Do NOT use `DM_Sans`, `--font-dm-sans`, or `DM Sans` in new code.
Fonts are loaded in `services/ui/src/lib/fonts.ts` and applied to
`<html>` in `app/layout.tsx`.

## Logo

- Use `<LeoLogo>` or `<LeoO>` from `@leo/design-system` for all
  wordmark / icon usages. Never use `<img src="/leo-icon.svg">`.
- Dark surfaces (sidebar, splash): `variant="dark"` (white letters).
- Light surfaces (home page, print): `variant="light"` (navy letters).
- Default spin is `spinning={true}` with `spinDuration={2.4}`.
- For loading states use `<LeoLoader>` or `<LeoSplash>` from
  `@leo/design-system`.

## Checking compliance

Static VT `brand-tokens-chrome.test.ts` asserts:
1. No file under `services/ui/src` imports `/leo-icon.svg`.
2. `AppShell.tsx` imports `LeoLogo` / `LeoO` from `@leo/design-system`.
3. `fonts.ts` uses `Albert_Sans` and `Overpass`, not `DM_Sans`.
4. No new hex values in the forbidden list above appear in the codebase.

## Design system as single source of truth

All brand tokens flow through `services/design-system/src/tokens/color.ts`
and `services/design-system/src/theme/index.ts`. A re-theme only ever
touches those files -- no scattered hex constants in UI components.
